      "problem": "Which of the following $x$-values is **not** in the domain of $y=\\tan x?$\n\n$$\n0, \\quad \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\quad \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}, \\quad \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254348/assets/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nThe domain of the function contains all real numbers except for $x= \\pm\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\pm\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2},\\dots$\n\nOf the given values, the only one that is **not** in the domain is  $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$",
